fonts-breip (1.0-8) experimental; urgency=low

  * Drop ttf-breip transitional package.
  * Drop leading capital from package description. Use
    "standard" debian-l10n-english formula "This package
    provides <foo>" in long description.
  * Add "Multi-Arch: foreign" field.
  * Update Standards to 3.9.4 (checked).
  * Use "Breaks" instead of "Conflicts". Drop "Provides" as it is no
    longer needed (installations should have transitioned since wheezy
    and the package has anyway no reverse dependency.
  * Drop useless Suggests on fontforge.
  * Use xz extreme compression for deb packages.
  * Use git for packaging: adapt Vcs-* fields.
  * Use Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends} to ensure that a versioned
    pre-dependency is esntually aded if needed (for instance on dpkg
    because of the use of an xz tarball).
  * Add myself to Uploaders.
  * Drop handling of defoma hints file in preinst.

